// Targeted therapy: EBV EBNA1 disruption in nasopharyngeal carcinoma.
//
// EBV (Epstein-Barr virus) persists as an episome in infected cells.
// EBNA1 is essential for episome maintenance — disrupt it and the
// viral genome is lost during cell division.
//
// The elegance: you don't need to cut every copy. You just need to
// break EBNA1. Without it, the episome can't replicate, and daughter
// cells dilute it out. The virus kills itself through the host's
// normal cell division.
//
// Sequence as drug:
//   1. AAV delivers CRISPR targeting EBNA1 coding sequence
//   2. Cells without EBV: no target, no effect
//   3. Cells with EBV: EBNA1 disrupted → episome maintenance fails
//   4. Over ~2 weeks of cell division, EBV genome dilutes to zero
//
// Real work: van Diemen et al. 2016, Yuen et al. 2015

target EBV_EBNA1 {
  organism human
  tolerance 0
  signatures GCTAGTCAACGATCCTG
  in only [ epithelial.cell ] @measured(human)
}

excise EBV_EBNA1
